Subject: [202605] Read AS7326 PSU output voltage limits from hardware

Port Edgecore's psu_v_out_min/max PDDF definitions for both PSU PMBus
interfaces. The existing driver decodes registers 0xa4/0xa5 and the platform
API converts millivolts to volts; no model-specific thresholds are hardcoded.
Source: https://github.com/edge-core/sonic-buildimage/blob/d39662e996c0e8748c9b96ad88dc5f5f524e8048/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/pddf/pddf-device.json

Validated on AS7326 with two FSF019-611 PSUs on 2026-11-13: after targeted
PMBus re-registration and pmon restart, both reported 11.390/12.593 V limits
through sysfs, the platform API and STATE_DB. Voltage health errors cleared.
PSU fan target/under-speed/over-speed APIs remain a separate open issue.
Verified upstream source: 5ef9e45ccf7f004fb07bf3f9be2f471cf00573bf.

--- a/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/pddf/pddf-device.json
+++ b/device/accton/x86_64-accton_as7326_56x-r0/pddf/pddf-device.json
@@ -204,6 +204,8 @@
